WEBVTT

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:17.830
8:00 on the dot. As always,
you're right on time, Mr. Doubt.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:20.740
Get a move on, Melancholy.

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:25.210
Wait up, Big Sis!

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:29.390
I'm sorry. It took some
time to get this one ready.

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:32.670
Not at all. I've only
just arrived myself.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.510
Miss Mizerka. Miss Melancholy.

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:38.100
Say, Sis...

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.430
Do you think this flower suits me?

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:41.930
Hey!

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:43.470
We're wasting time.

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:46.630
Let's get right to business, Mr. Whist.

00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:48.260
What the heck?!

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:50.400
I hate waste.

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:53.440
Japan has a lot of cute girls.

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:56.250
I stared so long that I got here late.

00:00:56.660 --> 00:01:00.110
Here. A sign of apology
for you young ladies.

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:02.240
No thank you.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:03.620
Such crude flowers!

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:05.590
Both those who arrive later than agreed,

00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:08.400
wasting other people's time...

00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:11.820
and those who arrive earlier than agreed,

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:17.240
thus wasting their own time, are fools, if you ask me.

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:20.470
I-I'm sorry I'm late, Freecell.

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:24.290
Rather than being late and
breaking an agreement,

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:28.050
it's much better to arrive
early and waste time.

00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:31.730
Agreements MUST be honored.

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:36.610
It would seem we are all here,

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:39.000
so I would share a few words with you...

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:44.680
Words from Klondike,

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:47.260
the leader of our Orpheus Order.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:04.910
Lost

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:08.030
Tesaguri de sagashiteta
I've searched, groping

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:11.950
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
The answer to a future that's been closed off

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:13.830
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
Is nowhere to be found

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:17.210
Hashiru shoudou, ima kaidoku funou
The impulse to run, it's impossible to decipher now

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:18.920
Found

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:23.130
Kudaketa hazu no unmei o
A fate that was supposedly smashed

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:27.640
Mijuku na yume no naka de kikoeta kitanda
I've come to hear it within that half-formed dream:

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:30.430
Saigo made I'll be there for you
Until the end, I'll be there for you

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:33.560
Tachidomaranai, kono hari dake wa
It won't stop, not this needle

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:36.900
Boku no asu o kizamu oto o tsukisasu
It will pierce the sound that engraves my tomorrow

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:38.770
Shinjitsu kara nigetara ima
If I run from the truth, then now...

00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:40.480
Genjitsu ni mo maketara ima
If I lose to reality, then now...

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:42.860
Nani ga nokoru no?
What will remain?

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:45.070
(Nokoru no?)
(Will remain?)

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:47.450
Kazoekirenai kono kizu dake ga
These countless wounds of mine

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:50.910
Boku no kinou o zanzou to shite kataru
They tell of my yesterday as an afterimage

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:52.620
Unmei ga hodoketemo ima
Even if fate were unraveled, now...

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:54.450
Sonzai o kowashitemo ima
Even if my existence were smashed, now...

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:57.290
Boku no michi o yuku yo
I will travel my path

00:02:57.870 --> 00:02:59.460
It's now or never

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:00.540
That is what they say

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:02.630
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:06.300
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:07.470
That is what they say

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:09.640
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:13.140
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:14.350
That is what they say

00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:16.770
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:22.970
Night of the Knights

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:33.230
Hey!

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:36.120
Not it.

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:37.070
You two!

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:40.190
This isn't it, either.

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:41.820
Hey, Nonoha!

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:44.040
What the heck are you doing?

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:45.560
It's obvious, isn't it?!

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:48.560
I'm making sure
no one's wearing a Ring.

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:49.450
Huh?

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:51.160
That earring and ring that acted

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:53.120
just like an Armlet of Orpheus

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:56.190
caused trouble for the vice
president and Airi, right?!

00:03:57.250 --> 00:04:00.710
Cube is still analyzing
the ring's remains,

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:04.280
and Ana is asking friends
to search all through town.

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:05.470
...would you tell me?

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:08.310
And the vice president and Airi are...

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:09.530
If you please...

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:11.020
If you please!

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:13.480
If this OWL
rings a BELL...
Student Council
Ah!!

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:12.720
If you please.

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:14.920
An owl?

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:16.840
It's an owl accessory.

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:18.980
It's quite dangerous if you put it on!

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:23.450
In any case, wearing accessories
is against school policy.

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:25.860
If you see it, please
let us know at once.

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:28.730
So, Kaito, you need to...

00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:31.440
Hey! That hair band!

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:32.790
Good grief.

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:40.530
I'm tired, somehow...

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:41.730
There, there.

00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:43.900
Well, walkin' around
with a face like THIS

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:45.220
will get ya tired.

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:46.970
I mean, come on!

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:49.560
Have you learned anything, Cubik?

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:51.520
This seems different from the

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.810
Armlet of Orpheus that Kaito and Rook had.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:55.310
What do you mean?

00:04:55.590 --> 00:04:58.700
There was a microchip invented only

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:00.700
very recently inside the remains.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:01.950
Very recently?

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:02.610
Yes.

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:06.180
The Armlets of Orpheus
should be ancient artifacts.

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:07.540
That means...

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:11.510
That this is a fake, made
by the Order of Orpheus?

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:14.080
I think "replica" would be more precise.

00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:16.520
Why would they make that?

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:18.670
Maybe they want to get good at puzzles.

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:21.560
They said they were collecting data.

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:22.800
Makes you wonder, doesn't it?

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:26.200
What they're after doesn't matter.

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:28.790
I can't forgive guys who'd use puzzles

00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:30.430
to hurt other people!

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:33.830
Agreed! I, Ana, cast my vote with you!

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:34.780
Me, too!

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:38.740
Well, goin' off half-cocked
will get us nowhere.

00:05:39.990 --> 00:05:41.820
If you want clues, we should wait

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:44.860
till someone puts on one of those Rings.

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:46.480
Gammon!

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:49.920
If someone puts a Ring on,
it could cost them their life!

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:52.530
We just have to solve the puzzle, right?

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:54.690
If we do, we can take it off.

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:56.870
The more awesome they make their puzzle,

00:05:56.870 --> 00:05:59.040
the more I look forward to it.

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:00.410
Gammon!

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:02.250
I swear...

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:05.520
Gammon may have a point.

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:07.880
Huh? Kaito, what are you saying?!

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:09.420
No matter what...

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:13.270
I can't believe they're
gonna keep lying low.

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:21.690
Hey, w-wait!

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:22.900
Show me your watch!

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:26.530
Look, give it a rest already!

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:29.210
Jeez.

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:37.870
It's him!

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:46.260
What's the matter?

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:47.620
Kaito!

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:49.840
This is bad!

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:51.970
I analyzed the Orpheus Ring

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:53.850
and searched for a signal.

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:55.010
And when I did...

00:06:55.520 --> 00:06:58.330
No way! These are all Ring signals?

00:06:58.330 --> 00:06:59.810
The Orpheus Order has spread them

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:02.190
out to people throughout town!

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:04.220
We have to get them all, fast!

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:06.180
Impossible. There are too many!

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:06.730
But-

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:08.890
Wait! This is a puzzle.

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:13.020
This blinking has three patterns.

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:16.990
If we overlap them and connect all the dots...

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:18.470
They're arrows!

00:07:18.970 --> 00:07:21.260
The place these arrows
are pointing to is...

00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:25.480
Don't tell me, that's...!

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:44.150
I'm back! Miharu, I'm home.

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:46.440
Welcome back, Brother.

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:49.540
Tonight's dinner is your favorite:

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:53.450
my special spicy tomato dumplings!

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:56.700
Say, Brother... What
do you think of THIS?

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:05.540
Gammon!

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:06.500
Gammon!

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:10.560
Sure enough, it was your
apartment building, huh?

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:11.690
This is bad!

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:14.300
Someone in there has an Orpheus Ring!

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:16.510
What's that?

00:08:18.230 --> 00:08:22.430
They gave a Ring to my
sister... to Miharu!

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:22.940
Huh?

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:23.770
So...?

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:25.030
She's fine.

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:27.090
I won't forgive 'em.

00:08:27.090 --> 00:08:29.310
They got Miharu
mixed up in this crap!

00:08:29.310 --> 00:08:31.030
I won't forgive 'em!

00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:33.120
Gammon...

00:08:33.690 --> 00:08:36.080
This was with the Ring.

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:41.740
"To the Phi-Brain Children,
Nippon Dome Stadium.

00:08:41.740 --> 00:08:44.460
The game begins at 18:00."

00:08:44.910 --> 00:08:47.830
This is... an invitation, for us.

00:08:55.530 --> 00:08:57.470
What about the scattered Orpheus Rings?

00:08:57.740 --> 00:09:01.350
It's all right. They were
all dummy transmitters.

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:15.070
It is 6:05.

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:16.670
You're five minutes late.

00:09:17.310 --> 00:09:19.330
It looks like you solved the puzzle.

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:23.200
It was a little bit of a
production, but did you like it?

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:26.900
What's the big idea, calling
us to a place like this?!

00:09:27.490 --> 00:09:30.260
You have made replicas
of the Armlets of Orpheus

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:32.660
and placed our students in harm's way.

00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:35.270
I would like to know why.

00:09:36.430 --> 00:09:37.900
I told you, didn't I?

00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:41.100
To free Man from the yoke of the Gods.

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:42.690
Dude...

00:09:42.690 --> 00:09:44.600
Using those replica Rings?

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:46.390
Perish the thought.

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:48.900
We shall make
the ultimate replica Ring.

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:54.390
You mean, you're trying to
artificially create a Ring

00:09:54.390 --> 00:09:56.260
with the same powers
as Armlets of Orpheus?

00:09:57.350 --> 00:09:58.860
I see.

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:01.120
Everything up till now was
an experiment for that.

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:02.170
Experiment?

00:10:02.170 --> 00:10:04.410
The replica rings the
vice president and Airi

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:07.370
were given were supposed to record data.

00:10:08.030 --> 00:10:09.260
I get it.

00:10:09.260 --> 00:10:12.800
You used them both to collect data

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:15.190
for getting as close to a
real Armlet as possible.

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:17.760
Bravo.

00:10:19.060 --> 00:10:20.520
We will strike at Kaito Daimon with

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:22.650
people whose minds have been

00:10:22.650 --> 00:10:24.750
forcefully activated via replica Rings.

00:10:24.750 --> 00:10:27.400
The stronger the opponent he fights,

00:10:27.400 --> 00:10:30.190
the better data we can collect. Right, Sis?

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:32.490
That's just cruel!

00:10:32.490 --> 00:10:34.860
The ultimate replica Ring...

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:38.640
Just what do you hope
to accomplish by creating it?

00:10:39.270 --> 00:10:42.370
We will distribute them to
people throughout the world.

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:45.510
This will allow all Mankind to awaken

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:48.910
the powers that have
been locked inside them.

00:10:49.570 --> 00:10:52.080
You mean, you'll use the Armlets

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:54.400
to forcibly raise Mankind's abilities?!

00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:57.300
We shall guide them. Humanity.

00:10:57.300 --> 00:11:00.380
But the experiment is on brief hiatus.

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:02.640
We're starting a new game.

00:11:02.950 --> 00:11:05.260
A new game. Namely...

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:08.020
Kaito Daimon: We shall destroy you.

00:11:08.020 --> 00:11:08.890
What?

00:11:17.180 --> 00:11:18.320
This is...?

00:11:28.180 --> 00:11:32.080
You cannot leave until
the game has been solved.

00:11:32.770 --> 00:11:35.120
I have prepared a new game, one even

00:11:35.120 --> 00:11:38.010
Mr. Freecell and the others
are unfamiliar with.

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:42.920
You get no credit if it's boring, Why.

00:11:43.340 --> 00:11:44.850
The name is "Whist".

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:49.300
I believe you're sure to
be satisfied, Miss Mela.

00:11:50.220 --> 00:11:53.150
It's Me-lan-cho-ly!

00:11:53.490 --> 00:11:55.480
We have not yet been introduced.

00:11:55.910 --> 00:11:58.320
I have been entrusted
with the personal care

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:02.610
of Mr. Freecell and the
others. I am Whist.

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:04.870
It's a pleasure to make
your acquaintance.

00:12:07.020 --> 00:12:09.850
The game is played four against four,

00:12:09.850 --> 00:12:12.080
a competition to steal
each other's territory.

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:14.920
I call it, "Lightning Position".

00:12:15.490 --> 00:12:17.920
Kaito Daimon and associates
comprise Red Team.

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:20.020
Mr. Doubt and associates
comprise Blue Team.

00:12:20.930 --> 00:12:23.700
Each side has five attacks
before changing turns.

00:12:23.700 --> 00:12:28.260
Players continue gameplay by
inheriting prior territories.

00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:33.690
Consulting or giving advice
within your teams is forbidden.

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:36.310
Contestants on the losing team...

00:12:42.820 --> 00:12:44.420
...shall meet THIS fate.

00:12:45.010 --> 00:12:47.870
Again... Another deadly puzzle?!

00:12:49.390 --> 00:12:52.450
I swear. You're pretty tacky, Why.

00:12:52.740 --> 00:12:54.770
Kaito. Everyone...

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:57.180
You and I are here,

00:12:57.180 --> 00:12:59.590
so why isn't this five vs. five?

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:02.420
You have no right to participate.

00:13:02.420 --> 00:13:03.550
What does that mean?

00:13:03.850 --> 00:13:06.260
You were not chosen by the Rings.

00:13:06.600 --> 00:13:10.100
You have no chance of becoming
a Phi-Brain, do you?

00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:14.180
Kaito Daimon...

00:13:14.690 --> 00:13:17.520
The man who came so
close to the Phi-Brain.

00:13:18.470 --> 00:13:19.750
Phi-Brain...

00:13:20.570 --> 00:13:24.180
One who is free from
the yoke of the Gods,

00:13:24.180 --> 00:13:27.420
has awakened to the true
power Humanity possesses.

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:30.380
If we beat you,

00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:33.330
we might be able to be Phi-Brains, too.

00:13:33.550 --> 00:13:35.670
You all, become Phi-Brains?

00:13:35.670 --> 00:13:38.280
We are Phi-Brain children, too.

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:40.740
Chosen by the Orpheus Rings.

00:13:40.740 --> 00:13:41.420
What?!

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:51.760
Th-those are...

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:54.010
Upperclassman Jikukawa, are they...?

00:13:54.010 --> 00:13:56.400
A-Armlets of Orpheus.

00:13:56.780 --> 00:13:59.000
And not replicas.

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:01.730
We are the real thing.

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:05.300
You all are Phi-Brain
children too, right?

00:14:05.300 --> 00:14:07.120
Let's do our best.

00:14:07.120 --> 00:14:10.190
Still, you don't have any Rings, though.

00:14:13.850 --> 00:14:16.370
Let's play up.

00:14:32.480 --> 00:14:33.390
Go ahead.

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:37.140
T-tails.

00:14:38.570 --> 00:14:42.770
Heads. Miss Melancholy and
the Blue Team go first.

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:47.780
Now then, first game: begin play.

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:51.370
Here I go.

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:55.200
Players move the same
way as knights in chess,

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:57.530
a right-angle path in four directions.

00:15:02.650 --> 00:15:04.150
In moving from your position,

00:15:04.150 --> 00:15:06.130
vertically, horizontally or diagonally,

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:07.560
you can change the color

00:15:07.560 --> 00:15:09.340
of the panels in eight directions.

00:15:17.230 --> 00:15:19.460
If you run into enemy panels,

00:15:19.460 --> 00:15:22.680
you make just one of them
yours and halt in place.

00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:29.650
Panels that have already been made

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:31.450
your color shall continue as-is.

00:16:01.910 --> 00:16:03.940
First game: The winner
is Miss Melancholy.

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:10.690
Honestly. You weren't even a challenge.

00:16:10.690 --> 00:16:12.820
Well, take care.

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:16.150
I'm sorry, everyone.

00:16:16.150 --> 00:16:18.810
What're you talkin' about?
We can still turn this around!

00:16:19.380 --> 00:16:21.430
And who is MY opponent?

00:16:28.440 --> 00:16:30.330
I, Ana, will go!

00:16:30.330 --> 00:16:31.720
Do us proud, Ana!

00:16:33.070 --> 00:16:36.900
Second game: The winner is Miss Mizerka.

00:16:39.910 --> 00:16:44.600
I, Ana, tried to make a face,
but I couldn't quite do it.

00:16:46.410 --> 00:16:48.110
Anyway, I'll be back!

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:54.450
Huh. I thought you'd come out last.

00:16:54.450 --> 00:16:57.030
I was asked in no uncertain terms.

00:16:58.680 --> 00:17:02.170
Well, order is of no consequence.

00:17:03.280 --> 00:17:06.590
If you were a girl, I'd take
it easy on you, though.

00:17:09.770 --> 00:17:11.640
Third game: Play.

00:17:20.090 --> 00:17:20.960
Here goes!

00:17:36.070 --> 00:17:40.090
Even if I take his territory,
he just takes it right back.

00:17:40.610 --> 00:17:42.710
I won't get anywhere at this rate.

00:17:48.650 --> 00:17:49.830
Oh.

00:17:51.820 --> 00:17:55.280
Third game: The winner is Mr. Pinochle.

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:57.960
We're up to just 10 points behind!

00:17:57.960 --> 00:17:59.390
Kaito, you're great!

00:17:59.620 --> 00:18:01.060
That's Kaito, all right!

00:18:01.610 --> 00:18:02.640
Still...

00:18:02.880 --> 00:18:05.110
Pinochole. That was unsightly.

00:18:05.590 --> 00:18:06.840
You're the worst!

00:18:06.840 --> 00:18:08.340
What's more, the final move

00:18:08.340 --> 00:18:10.060
was a mistake by Kaito Daimon.

00:18:10.260 --> 00:18:12.800
Mistake? Is that right?

00:18:12.800 --> 00:18:15.720
True, he would've been
able to get more territory

00:18:15.720 --> 00:18:18.280
if he'd moved to a different spot.

00:18:18.790 --> 00:18:22.660
That was rather helpful, Kaito Daimon.

00:18:24.890 --> 00:18:26.650
Kaito made a mistake?

00:18:26.650 --> 00:18:28.250
Is that possible?

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:47.810
Gammon Sakanoue.

00:18:47.810 --> 00:18:51.350
The man selected by
Rook Banjo Crossfield.

00:18:51.350 --> 00:18:53.230
As a stepping stone for the purpose

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:55.280
of raising Kaito Daimon as a Phi-Brain.

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:58.450
Your whole existence is a waste, worm.

00:18:58.850 --> 00:19:00.570
I'll finish this thing quickly.

00:19:01.560 --> 00:19:03.620
Now then, the last game.

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:04.750
Play.

00:19:10.840 --> 00:19:14.350
I'll have you apologize for
involving my younger sister!

00:19:16.680 --> 00:19:20.130
Sister? Oh, you mean THAT.

00:19:20.420 --> 00:19:22.920
I couldn't care less how that turned out.

00:19:22.920 --> 00:19:24.050
What?!

00:19:24.480 --> 00:19:28.890
Rather, if it proved
useful to our goals...

00:19:29.160 --> 00:19:31.490
That shallow existence served

00:19:31.490 --> 00:19:34.400
some small purpose in having been born.

00:19:35.780 --> 00:19:39.400
Then I'm gonna make you
regret having been born!

00:19:39.950 --> 00:19:42.410
Being born and meeting ME!

00:19:58.820 --> 00:20:00.010
We caught up to them!

00:20:08.720 --> 00:20:09.520
Dammit!

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:11.230
They pulled out in front again.

00:20:16.370 --> 00:20:18.020
There are five paths I can take.

00:20:18.900 --> 00:20:21.110
The one that gets me the most panels is...

00:20:24.490 --> 00:20:25.560
HERE!

00:20:30.930 --> 00:20:31.790
What's this?

00:20:32.260 --> 00:20:33.480
A tie?!

00:20:42.530 --> 00:20:44.370
Whist! What's the meaning of this?

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:47.890
Let's leave today's game as a draw.

00:20:50.600 --> 00:20:52.820
Kaito really is incredible.

00:20:52.820 --> 00:20:54.500
What do you mean?

00:20:54.500 --> 00:20:56.310
He made a mistake.

00:20:56.550 --> 00:20:58.350
Even if you change a panel's color,

00:20:58.350 --> 00:21:00.540
it can soon be taken back.

00:21:00.540 --> 00:21:03.580
Simply repeating that
is meaningless, yes?

00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:07.370
Huh.

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:09.850
Yes. That's why Kaito made choosing

00:21:09.850 --> 00:21:11.790
panels that were difficult to take back,

00:21:11.790 --> 00:21:13.660
rather than getting as many panels

00:21:13.660 --> 00:21:14.960
at once, his priority.

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:17.330
The panels on the game board's periphery.

00:21:17.940 --> 00:21:21.130
Those panels stayed red till the end.

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:22.880
So that's it?

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:24.880
He didn't make a mistake at all.

00:21:24.880 --> 00:21:26.500
Great job, Kaito!

00:21:26.500 --> 00:21:27.880
You're so smart!

00:21:27.880 --> 00:21:29.850
Kaito's an idiot.

00:21:29.850 --> 00:21:32.390
You shouldn't underestimate him.

00:21:32.390 --> 00:21:33.540
Even though he's an idiot.

00:21:33.540 --> 00:21:34.850
Quit sayin' "idiot" already!

00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:36.550
Kaito Daimon...

00:21:36.550 --> 00:21:38.160
He's the same as always.

00:21:38.160 --> 00:21:40.570
Indeed. Just like the old days.

00:21:40.570 --> 00:21:41.980
He still pisses me off.

00:21:42.910 --> 00:21:44.490
What're you talkin' about?

00:21:45.310 --> 00:21:47.620
You still can't remember?

00:21:48.240 --> 00:21:50.830
Can't... remember?

00:21:51.890 --> 00:21:54.190
Let's meet again, Kaito.

00:22:00.520 --> 00:22:01.520
Everyone!

00:22:01.520 --> 00:22:02.380
Kaito!

00:22:16.510 --> 00:22:19.980
Mama. Kaito hasn't changed at all.

00:22:20.410 --> 00:22:24.240
Just like before, he's good at puzzles.

00:22:24.240 --> 00:22:25.970
Like that time before, he was...

00:22:26.690 --> 00:22:28.210
Ruthless.

00:22:38.710 --> 00:22:40.050
Eiyuukidori
Playing the hero

00:22:40.050 --> 00:22:44.940
Itsudatte shinjita muteki no kankaku
A sense of invincibility you always believed in

00:22:45.550 --> 00:22:51.370
Tatakatte iru no wa chikyuu no tame nanka ja nai
You're not fighting for the sake of the world or anything

00:22:51.370 --> 00:22:54.160
Motto maipeesu de
It's for a more leisurely

00:22:54.160 --> 00:22:59.230
Sou, motto shoujiki na onegai no tame
Yeah, more straightforward request

00:22:59.600 --> 00:23:07.670
Nandotonaku kizutsuitemo tachiagare, hero
Even if you're wounded over and over, rise up, hero

00:23:07.670 --> 00:23:13.220
Kitto daijoubu, kimi o mamorunda
It's sure to be all right, I'll protect you

00:23:13.610 --> 00:23:17.040
Machigai da to shitemo tomarenai
Even if it's wrong, it can't be stopped

00:23:17.040 --> 00:23:20.650
Seikai ka nante wakaranai
I don't know if it's the right answer

00:23:21.550 --> 00:23:24.660
Donna toki demo original ni
No matter the situation

00:23:24.660 --> 00:23:27.400
Step o fumidashiteku
I'll take those first steps, originally

00:23:27.400 --> 00:23:30.770
Dramatic ni, mawaru sekai de
On this spinning world, I'm searching, dramatically

00:23:30.770 --> 00:23:34.430
Kiwameita wonder sagashiteru
For wonders that sparkle

00:23:35.190 --> 00:23:38.430
Boku, shijou saikou no tabi o tsuzukeyou
Me, I'll keep going on the greatest journey in history

00:23:38.430 --> 00:23:42.740
Image shite shiawase na mirai e
To the happy future I imagined

00:23:44.430 --> 00:23:46.060
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:51.380
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:51.380 --> 00:23:52.800
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:54.710 --> 00:23:56.260
(Mirai e)
(To the future)

00:24:02.700 --> 00:24:03.800
This is bad!

00:24:03.800 --> 00:24:05.970
Gammon is angry and
there's no calming him down!

00:24:05.970 --> 00:24:09.870
I, Ana, think that Gammon is hungry!

00:24:09.870 --> 00:24:12.290
Let's make eat lots of food!

00:24:12.290 --> 00:24:15.500
Uh, that's not it. It's about Miharu-

00:24:15.500 --> 00:24:16.440
I get it!

00:24:16.440 --> 00:24:18.490
He's not getting enough calcium.

00:24:18.490 --> 00:24:20.260
Let's make him drink milk!

00:24:20.260 --> 00:24:22.930
Next time,
"Wandering Galileo"

00:24:22.930 --> 00:24:25.310
Okay, let's give him some cheese!
